\f1\b \cf0 \strokec2 Key Translation Points:
\f0\b0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 allocate
\f1\fs24  vs. 
\f3\fs26 new
\f1\fs24 :
\f0\b0  The Fortran 
\f2\fs26 allocate(..., source=0)
\f0\fs24  is translated to 
\f2\fs26 CommonGlobals.array = new type[size]
\f0\fs24 . Java automatically initializes new numeric arrays to 0 or 0.0, so the 
\f2\fs26 source=0
\f0\fs24  behavior is implicit.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The single case of 
\f2\fs26 source=1.0d0
\f0\fs24  requires an extra step using 
\f2\fs26 Arrays.fill()
\f0\fs24 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f3\b\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 resize
\f1\fs24  Return Value:
\f0\b0  As noted before, the Java 
\f2\fs26 Resize
\f0\fs24  methods 
\f1\b return
\f0\b0  the new array. The caller 
\f4\i must
\f0\i0  assign this returned value back to the global variable, e.g., 
\f2\fs26 CommonGlobals.nsm = Resize.resize_int1(CommonGlobals.nsm, CommonGlobals.NMOD);
\f0\fs24 .\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Array Indexing:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ncc(3,NSLS)
\f0\fs24  becomes 
\f2\fs26 new double[3][CommonGlobals.NSLS]
\f0\fs24 .\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f2\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 axisgr(0:3,3,NGR)
\f0\fs24  (which means sizes 4, 3, and NGR) becomes 
\f2\fs26 new double[4][3][CommonGlobals.NGR]
\f0\fs24 . This is consistent with how 
\f2\fs26 resize_double0
\f0\fs24  was implemented.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
