\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 Important Notes on This Translation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Matrix Inversion (
\f3\fs26 invten
\f1\fs24 ):
\f0\b0  The 
\f2\fs26 invten
\f0\fs24  subroutine is 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  translated. I have created a stub method 
\f2\fs26 TensorUtils.invten()
\f0\fs24 . You 
\f1\b must
\f0\b0  provide a real 6x6 matrix inversion implementation here. Using a library like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://commons.apache.org/proper/commons-math/"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \ul \ulc4 \strokec4 Apache Commons Math}} is highly recommended.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 File I/O:
\f0\b0  The Fortran 
\f2\fs26 WRITE(11,...)
\f0\fs24  and 
\f2\fs26 OPEN(77,...)
\f0\fs24  calls are translated using Java's 
\f2\fs26 PrintWriter
\f0\fs24 . You 
\f1\b must
\f0\b0  call 
\f2\fs26 IOUtils.initializeWriters()
\f0\fs24  
\f4\i once
\f0\i0  at the beginning of your program before 
\f2\fs26 avModulus
\f0\fs24  or 
\f2\fs26 backStress
\f0\fs24  is called.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Array Indexing (Critical):
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This code (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 do ng=1,ngrain
\f0\fs24 ) relies on 
\f1\b 1-based indexing
\f0\b0 .\
\ls4\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 This means your allocatable arrays (
\f2\fs26 wgt
\f0\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 ccs2
\f0\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 nact
\f0\fs24 , etc.) 
\f1\b must
\f0\b0  be allocated with size 
\f2\fs26 [N+1]
\f0\fs24  (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 new double[NGR+1]
\f0\fs24 ) to avoid 
\f2\fs26 ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
\f0\fs24 .\
\ls4\ilvl1\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Please 
\f1\b review the 
\f3\fs26 AllocationRoutines.java
\f1\fs24  file
\f0\b0  I sent previously. All allocations (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 new int[CommonGlobals.NGR]
\f0\fs24 ) should be changed to 
\f2\fs26 new int[CommonGlobals.NGR + 1]
\f0\fs24 , and all resize calls (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 resize_int1(..., CommonGlobals.NGR)
\f0\fs24 ) should be changed to 
\f2\fs26 resize_int1(..., CommonGlobals.NGR + 1)
\f0\fs24 .\
