\cf0 \strokec2 You've provided the missing 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 invten
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  implementation, which is great! This subroutine, along with its helpers 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 LUDCMPC
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  and 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 LUBKSBC
\f0\fs24 \strokec2 , is a Java translation of the LU decomposition method for matrix inversion.\
This code 
\f1\b \strokec2 replaces the stub
\f0\b0 \strokec2  for 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 invten
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  I provided in the 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 TensorUtils.java
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  class.\
There is one function, 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 TNORM
\f0\fs24 \strokec2 , that was used in 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 INVTEN
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  but not provided. I have created a stub for it with a 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 TODO
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  note. You will need to implement this function based on your program's requirements (it's likely a function to find the maximum absolute value of the matrix).\
Here is the updated 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 TensorUtils.java
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  class containing the complete, translated code.\
Here is the translation for the 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 mod_cr_to_sa
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  module and the 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 cr_to_sa
\f0\fs24 \strokec2  subroutine.\
This code performs tensor rotations to transform physical properties from the crystal's coordinate system (CR) to the lab/sample's coordinate system (SA) using the grain's orientation (rotation matrix 
\f2\fs26 \strokec2 r
\f0\fs24 \strokec2 ).\
